  "graph": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "Study: a pattern-based studio (channel rack, step sequencer, piano roll, playlist), rebuilt with pattern banks, accents, and swing.\n\nFour drum channels play slices of one sample from one Pattern with two banks, A and B. Its hat row carries accents (levels set by dragging a cell up or down) into the hat Sampler's velocity, and the Sixteenths clock swings, so every drum swings with it. A chord channel and a bass channel play from MIDI Patterns (piano rolls); the chords have banks A and B too. One Clock gate is the playlist. Each channel has volume, pan, and mute on a Track block. The Beat panel is the grid and the piano roll, edited while they play; the Rack panel is the channel rack's knobs and mutes.\n\nWhat the real thing has that this can't: a playlist you draw patterns onto, per-step pitch inside the grid, and a fill button. Read docs/GAPS.md."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            0.0,
            -560.0
          ],
          "size": [
            760.0,
            230.0
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "3",
        "kind": "clock",
        "params": {
          "interval": 0.25,
          "swing": 0.3
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            0.0,
            -120.0
          ],
          "label": "Sixteenths"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "39",
        "kind": "clock",
        "params": {
          "duty": 0.5,
          "interval": 32.0,
          "offset": 16.0
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            0.0,
            -300.0
          ],
          "label": "Every other four bars"
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "6",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "The playlist: a Clock 32 beats long whose gate is high for its second half (offset 16), so the Pattern's and the chords' bank is 1, pattern B, in bars 5 to 8 of every eight. A bank changes where its next pass begins, so B starts on the bar line, and from any bar the song is played from."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            600.0,
            -300.0
          ],
          "size": [
            466.0,
            80.0
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "7",
